# Top-level dependencies. This is the INPUT for rebuilding constraints.txt --
# what gets installed on the machine is constraints.txt; see its header.
#
# Pinning is mandatory for two reasons at once. First: without it, dependency
# resolution happens on a rented machine during a run. The second is left from
# the era of layers -- installing in parts without pinning meant each part
# demolished the previous one: torch deleted the CUDA libraries installed
# before it and downloaded its own, and the deleted files stayed in the lower
# layer as 1.48 GB of dead weight.
